    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T10:13:14Z",
    "body": "Escalated to effort:medium by issue-worker-low (claude-haiku-5-5); claim released, nothing pushed.\n\nWhat was learned:\n- The shell's Image widgets paint as textured Mesh shapes in epaint 0.36 (`Shape::Image` does not exist), so the painted check walks `Shape::Mesh` and reads `texture_id`.\n- The icon set is up in the kittest once a frame has run (`IconSet::load` in the shell test frame), so the texture ids are real.\n- Painting the Tool library page is not enough: the catalog row `BN-0600` paints no ball-nose glyph (29 textures painted, not the full catalog), because egui drops shapes outside the clip rect and the catalog sits in a clipped scroll area. A taller harness window did not help. The fix needs the catalog's painted rows reached (scroll the catalog into view, or assert per visible row) before the test can cover all rows.\n- The picker pass (`tool_combo` in op_page) is not written yet; it needs an operation page with the dropdown opened.\n\nHeld work: none pushed; the branch was local only and is removed. The approach above is the starting point for the medium tier.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
